  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "The three bin labels are fixed as how, when, where. Never change the words or their order.",
      "Every stem is one kid-world sentence with exactly one target adverb. Never write two adverbs in one stem.",
      "The target adverb must be manner (how), time (when), or place (where). Never use degree words such as very, too, really, almost, or only as the target.",
      "Do not use together, also, still, or already as the target adverb.",
      "Keep the filled pool near one third how, one third when, and one third where.",
      "Wrong-bin taps are the other two labels only. Never add a fourth choice.",
      "Tier 1: short stem, obvious adverb at the end, picture lemma on a concrete noun.",
      "Tier 3: near-miss adverbs such as hard, well, home, first, always, down, or above."
    ]
  },
